<BaseLayout title="Differential" description="Ford 8.8 IRS kit and custom DSS axles for high-horsepower Genesis Coupe LS swaps.">
  <h1>Differential</h1>

  <h2>Ford 8.8 IRS (High HP)</h2>
  <p>
    For builds targeting 1000+ hp, Jason Riddle's Ford 8.8 IRS kit is the documented path that avoids axle failures under hard launches.
    The kit replaces the stock differential and requires custom axles from The Driveshaft Shop (DSS).
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>DSS axle requirements:</strong> Send your wheel hubs so DSS can broach them from 30-spline to 33-spline.
    Measure seal-to-bearing (hub) carefully:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Driver side:</strong> ~23.25&quot; (closer to 23-3/8&quot;)</li>
    <li><strong>Passenger side:</strong> ~24.25&quot; (closer to 24-3/8&quot;)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Reference order (English Rob / Robert Kapeluch, DSS invoice 114850): Side A 23.5&quot; Seal-to-BB, Side B 24.25&quot; Seal-to-BB, 108mm-30 outer CVs with GKN grease caps.
    Customer sends OEM wheel hubs to be broached to 33-spline.
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong>Install video:</strong>
    <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/t/ZTfag4jc8/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TikTok — Ford 8.8 IRS install</a>
  </p>

